BBUUGGSS
       SSLLIISSTT__FFOORREEAACCHH()  doesn’t  allow  _v_a_r  to be removed or freed within the
       loop, as it would interfere with the traversal.   SSLLIISSTT__FFOORREEAACCHH__SSAAFFEE(),
       which  is  present  on the BSDs but is not present in glibc, fixes this
       limitation by allowing _v_a_r to safely be removed from the list and freed
       from within the loop without interfering with the traversal.

